    <div class="p8-section-label">Phase 8 · Complete System Specification</div>
    <h2 class="p8-section-title">40kWh plug-in · solar roof array · dual-rail steam · 6-alternator regen</h2>
    <p class="p8-section-lead">
        Phase 8 solves the energy source problem cleanly. A 40kWh lithium EV battery pack
        (Battery A) replaces the AGM unit, bringing enough stored energy for 200+ miles of
        steam-powered driving on a single charge. Grid charging via a standard J1772 port
        fills the pack overnight. An integrated roof solar array — with optional front and
        rear hood mod panels — provides continuous renewable top-up. The six alternators
        from Phase 7 stay in place, their recovered energy extending range further.
        Battery B (LiFePO₄ 200Ah) remains dedicated to the backup EV motor and emergency systems.
    </p>

